{
  "name": "vector_light_shader_max",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "\u00a727 phase 6: the max evaluated PER FRAGMENT on the visibility polygon's own triangle fan, against phase 5's per-cell version and against #151 as originally built. One midnight room, one torch, one OPEN DOOR \u2014 which is the scene #151 never shot. Its measurement was taken on an open APERTURE, where both lighting models walk the same straight line through the hole and the max correctly wins nothing; probed here, the peak lift is 7 levels of glow through an aperture and 70 through a door, because RimWorld's glow grid never learns a door opened. Seven arms: vanilla, phase 3's mask alone, the shipped flat beam, phase 5's per-cell max, #151's composition exactly (no mask, no suppression, vanilla untouched underneath, the shader adding max(0, ours - vanilla)), phase 6 (the mask carving the shadow at cell resolution and the shader setting the level at polygon resolution), and the control, which is the same shader with its subtraction off \u2014 max(0, ours - 0) is MoteGlow's output exactly, so any difference there is the shader rather than the composition. vector_light_shader_max_available is pinned in every arm that claims to use the shader: standing down is by design silent, and --mod-overlay swaps assemblies only, so a bundle that never reached the run leaves every other number healthy while the frames quietly show the previous composition.",
